From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kk: report format capabilities and texel classes on rejected views

STEAMAC-G/A has seven RGBA8 -> R8 view rejections and one BC3_UNORM ->
RGBA8_SRGB rejection. On an M1 Max, both R8 and RGBA8 report identical
linear/optimal features (0x40018001dd83), buffer features (0x180000058),
and successful exact usage 0x480097 / mutable-format queries. R8 clears
and every readback byte pass at 1664/1920/1952x288 with those usages.
Neither the pinned guest Zink format selector nor its resource creation
has an R8 -> RGBA8 fallback. The producer remains unproven, and substituting
a different format would not preserve the requested pixels.

BC3 has a 16-byte compressed block, RGBA8 a 4-byte texel: even adding
BLOCK_TEXEL_VIEW_COMPATIBLE does not make those formats compatible. The
flag survives vk_image_init and the tested 0x88 request reaches the
rejection unchanged; legal BC3 sRGB and 16-byte RGBA32_UINT block views
still create. The reported flags 0x8 do not establish a dropped flag.

Extend 0095 only on rejected views: report actual image/view format
features and their differences, external-memory types, block dimensions
and sizes, and the block-texel-compatible bit. No extra work on successful
views, new allocation, substitute backing, or changed rejection semantics.
This is diagnostic, not a resolution of the guest context failure.

Regression: REPRO_CASE=sentry-g-views REPRO_DRIVER=kosmickrisp
host/moltenvk/repro/run.sh <dylib>. The diagnostic assertions fail before
this patch and pass after under Metal API validation; all 26 view cases,
three R8 clear/readbacks, and four exact-format property queries pass.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
index 175ddeb..3f18c03 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
@@ -70,6 +70,29 @@ kk_log_image_view_request(struct kk_device *dev, const struct kk_image *image,
              info->components.g, info->components.b, info->components.a,
              range->aspectMask, range->baseMipLevel, range->levelCount,
              range->baseArrayLayer, range->layerCount);
+   const VkFormat format = info->format == VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED
+                              ? image->vk.format : info->format;
+   struct kk_physical_device *pdev = kk_device_physical(dev);
+   VkFormatFeatureFlags2 image_features = kk_get_image_format_features(
+      pdev, image->vk.format, image->vk.tiling, 0);
+   VkFormatFeatureFlags2 view_features = kk_get_image_format_features(
+      pdev, format, image->vk.tiling, 0);
+   mesa_loge("kk: image view format features image=0x%llx view=0x%llx "
+             "image-only=0x%llx view-only=0x%llx external=0x%x",
+             (unsigned long long)image_features,
+             (unsigned long long)view_features,
+             (unsigned long long)(image_features & ~view_features),
+             (unsigned long long)(view_features & ~image_features),
+             image->vk.external_handle_types);
+   mesa_loge("kk: image view texel blocks image=%ux%u/%uB view=%ux%u/%uB "
+             "block-texel-compatible=%u",
+             vk_format_get_blockwidth(image->vk.format),
+             vk_format_get_blockheight(image->vk.format),
+             vk_format_get_blocksize(image->vk.format),
+             vk_format_get_blockwidth(format), vk_format_get_blockheight(format),
+             vk_format_get_blocksize(format),
+             !!(image->vk.create_flags &
+                VK_IMAGE_CREATE_BLOCK_TEXEL_VIEW_COMPATIBLE_BIT));
    const VkBaseInStructure *ext = info->pNext;
    for (unsigned i = 0; ext && i < 8; i++, ext = ext->pNext) {
       if (ext->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_VIEW_USAGE_CREATE_INFO) {
